WEBVTT

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.660
Men, don’t let anyone near until
we’re done inspecting the site.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.110
Understood!

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.580
Absolutely nothing survived...

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.000
And here we almost had it!

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.230
Chizuru Yukimura

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.260
And? Where has Kodo-san gone?

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.930
We don’t know!

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.000
His body never turned up, so there

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.020
is a chance he survived, but...

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.020
They were entering and leaving
headquarters a lot of late.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.530
There is a possibility that
the national loyalists

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.580
were suspicious of his relationship
to us and attacked him.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:19.750
I see...

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.910
At any rate,

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.330
we must investigate
whether the secret about

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.390
the Water of Life we had been working on

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.770
under Shogunal orders has been leaked.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.250
You’re right...

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.690
In any event, we should make finding
Kodo-san our top priority.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.470
Speaking of which, Kondou-san,

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.350
in regards to Serizawa-san.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.810
How do you intend to carry out
the Aizu Domain’s orders?

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.690
Why not simply have him
relinquish his position as chief?

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:54.070
There’s no way that man
would go along with that!

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.340
I will try speaking with Serizawa-san.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.040
Hey, seriously?

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.450
We’ve had chats with
him several times in the past!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.460
He’s the one who always goes
against everything we say!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.300
But he is a fellow
warrior who came to the

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.080
If I logically explain our reasoning,

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.300
capital embracing the same ideals as us!

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.680
he should come around!

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:22.680
A Moonlit Night Filled
with Flowers

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.430
Blood! Give me blood!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.800
N-Niimi-san, my-my throat!

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.110
My throat burns!

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.400
It-it hurts!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.440
Wait, I’ll give you the medicine now.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.690
Pipe down!

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:42.690
I’ll administer the
medicine in a minute.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.700
Open your mouth and sit still!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.960
Here, drink some water.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.130
Give some to me!

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.710
I know! I’ll give you
some soon, so just wait!

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.720
So when their bloodlust hits,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.000
this medicine makes
it possible for them

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.770
to hang onto their sanity by a thread.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.610
Please save me!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.200
I-I can’t take this much longer!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.200
Please just kill me!

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.990
Bear with it a while longer.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.120
I will make a better medicine shortly.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.490
Niimi-san! Niimi-san!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:25.870
Niimi-san...!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.360
Considering their condition,

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.670
I couldn’t possibly take them with me.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.640
This way, please.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.480
I’ve kept you waiting.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.120
Hardly! I just arrived myself.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.190
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.650
I am coming in.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.610
Here you go.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.440
Uh, no thanks. I’m sorry,

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.030
but could you take your leave?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.130
Sure, in that case...

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.250
Take your time.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:22.170
To be honest, the reason
why I called you here today

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.430
was in regards to the
Shinsengumi’s future.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.760
Here we came to the red-light district

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.250
and you want to jump straight into

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.130
work without so much as a drink first?

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.480
What an inconsiderate oaf!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.930
That’s because...

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.980
I am terribly sorry.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.310
Here you go.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.320
You aren’t even calling for a geisha?

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:53.290
Serizawa-san, we have been appointed
the title “Shinsengumi”

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.080
and were officially entrusted with
conducting patrols around Kyoto.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:59.330
What of it?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.190
We have been charged
to protect the peace,

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.590
so you must refrain from conducting any

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.270
further unscrupulous behavior.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:07.430
Oh?

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.520
If you continue as you
have, Serizawa-san,

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.560
I will have no choice but make
you relinquish your title!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.850
Why did you deliberately divulge
that information with me?

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.640
Wouldn’t it be a dream
come true for you

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.760
and your men if you
became the sole chief,

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:26.580
with the Aizu Domain as your sponsor?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.400
Well?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.660
I believe that the two
of us, Serizawa-san,

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.710
should continue to steer
the Shinsengumi together!

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.050
True, there has been
friction between us,

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.630
but I am grateful to you, Serizawa-san!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.030
That’s why--

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.650
That is not something you should say to

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.250
the person you are negotiating with.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.160
tHuh?

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.890
If your goal is to run a small dojo,

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.480
that may be taken as virtuous.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.350
However, those are not the
words of a feudal lord.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:01.510
I realized a long time
ago that I lack the

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.390
ability to serve as a general.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.340
But Toshi--

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.290
He said that he believes
in my potential!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.140
That’s why!

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:15.910
Do you have any idea why Hijikata
holds you in such high regard?

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:21.460
That man is living his
dream through you.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.110
His hopes and dreams
to live as a samurai...

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.200
He was entrusted them in a man: you.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.190
However, I imagine that someday those
views will bring you anguish.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.930
What do you mean by that?

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.260
It means just as it sounds.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.110
If you remain chief of the Shinsengumi,

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.900
you will take the brunt of the
national loyalists’ hatred.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:54.700
Do you have what it will
take to withstand that?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.020
I formed my resolve!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.950
I will make the Shinsengumi
grow into something big!

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:02.100
As long as everyone who believed in me

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.130
and accompanied me here
shares that dream,

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.370
I can continue to run
along Toshi’s side!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:10.960
Now, then...

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.180
That is enough of this
stifling conversation.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.240
Hey, server!

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.650
Do you need something?

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.150
Fetch a geisha.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.150
Yes, sir.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.050
A moment, Serizawa-san!

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:28.480
We aren’t done talking.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:29.980
Uh, sirs?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.610
Hurry it up!

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.530
S-sir...

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.460
Serizawa-san, please promise
to change your ways!

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.720
Serizawa-san!

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:47.970
Hirama-san, I finished
with the cleaning.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.330
Oh, I appreciate it.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.730
Oh, right! Ibuki-kun, would you mind

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.300
taking that saké to the master?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.350
Sure, I don’t mind.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.980
Don’t you intend to kill me anymore?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:03.810
I wouldn’t mind.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:08.900
Dying by your hands
wouldn’t be so bad.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.440
Sorry to hear that.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.820
After failing to kill you the other day,

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.540
I’ve lost all interest in it.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:18.320
That right?

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.080
It is.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.020
But why do you leave
yourself exposed like this

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.580
before a woman who tried to kill you?

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:29.550
All humans die eventually anyway.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.330
It’s just a matter of whether
it is sooner or later.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.060
Besides, you resemble her.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:40.850
Who?

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:45.530
The first woman I ever... loved.

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:49.180
No, she was also the
last woman I ever loved.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.150
What type of person was she?

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.170
She was shunned by the world,

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.790
yet even when treated
as if she didn’t exist

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:03.460
she still tried her damnedest to live.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:08.120
What is that lady doing now?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.510
She died long ago.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:13.080
An illness made her
grow unable to remember

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.780
who she was or recognize
me or anyone else.

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:18.910
A few years after the woman died,

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:23.760
I learned that I had been
infected with the same disease.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:28.650
Normally people grieve when they
contract a fatal disease,

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.150
but for some reason, it made me happy.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:34.650
Do you know why?

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.740
I can die of the same
disease as that woman.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.830
That’s what I thought.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.130
Even I recognize how horribly
effeminate that thought is.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.470
There is no way that
a man such as I could

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:53.820
possibly go to the same Paradise

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.790
as that woman.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.430
Perhaps it is because the first woman

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.910
I fell in love with was one such as her,

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.550
but I developed the belief
that the “truth”

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:06.930
is born from planting
its roots deep below

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.420
while the top gets covered with mud.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.640
Such is my belief.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.780
With its beautiful flowers
blooming above the mud...

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.450
...it is just like a lotus.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.080
Ryunosuke!

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.590
Have you seen Niimi-san?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:40.670
Nope, I haven’t seen him today.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.050
Is there a problem?

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.430
He’s gone!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.970
He took the Water of Life and vanished!

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:48.980
He what?!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.650
I suspected that he’d try to pull
something sooner or later,

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.580
but to think he ran off
with the Water of Life.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.450
What should we do, Hijikata-san?

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:02.290
Don’t we need to hurry
and find out where he went?

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.950
Considering the weight of the situation,

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:09.660
I’d love to send all of our
men out to find Niimi-san.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.000
But with the Water of
Life in the picture,

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.420
I can only send the
handful of us that know

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.170
about the medicine to look for him.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.840
Indeed.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.710
Fortunately, he did not
take the men he turned

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.680
into furies and experimented on.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:28.380
Which means that if Niimi-san
doesn’t resume his experiments,

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:31.310
we won’t hear of any trouble
from him anytime soon, huh?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:35.090
But wouldn’t that man do whatever it

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:37.190
takes to sell the Water of Life?

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.080
Anyway, finding Niimi-san
is our top priority.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:45.200
Keep your eyes peeled when
you conduct your patrols.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.500
Sir!

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:27.880
Commander!

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.840
Yamazaki? What is it?

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.370
Come in.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.240
Pardon me.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.300
What is it?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.630
I came across a rumor
that caught my attention.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.830
There has been an outbreak
of bizarre murders

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.050
throughout town the past few days.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.070
Bizarre murders?

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:50.390
Correct.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.390
According to the locals, the bodies

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.830
have been drained of
most of their blood.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:56.950
What?!

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.280
I got it! Here’s your saké!

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.650
The cur, eh?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.790
You took too long!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:12.790
Thank you for getting that.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.290
I’ll take over from here.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:17.050
Uh, okay...

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.540
Hey, dog!

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:27.220
Do you know of a man named Iori Tanaka?

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:30.640
Iori Tanaka? Who’s that?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.430
Supposedly that man
held a drinking party

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.580
in Shimabara with some
national loyalist

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.690
ronin the other day.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:39.690
Huh?

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.810
According to the head clerk that

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:43.940
led them to their banquet room,

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.290
that man claimed to have “an ace up

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.950
his sleeve to expel the foreigners.”

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:54.660
His style of speech and his
voice sounded just like Niimi.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:56.490
What?!

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.960
Where is he--where is that
Iori Tanaka guy right now?

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:00.820
Beats me.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:04.570
I see.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.830
So you mean to say that there
is a possibility that Niimi-san

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:10.030
changed his name and approached

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:12.500
national loyalist ronin, yes?

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.600
You did good to inform us, Ibuki-kun.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.580
Nah, this all came from Serizawa-san.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.290
I didn’t do anything.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:25.260
But how did Serizawa-san
manage to simply

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.010
come across that information?

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:27.610
Huh?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.590
We dedicated over half a month to

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.510
finding him only to
come up empty handed...

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.250
Yamazaki!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:36.040
Sir!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.170
Go investigate Shimabara immediately.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.620
Very well.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:41.350
How’s it look?

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.270
One jab right to the heart.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.470
Musta been a fatal blow.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.590
Anyway, we ought to get
him out of the water.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.680
Hey, put this dead guy over there!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.470
What’s goin’ on?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.730
No one is to go beyond this point!

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.770
Are you certain he was a fury?

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.660
I am. I believe the
experiment failed and

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.710
he could no longer control the fury,

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.270
thus he killed the man.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.780
What should we do, Hijikata-san?

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.490
Commander!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.490
What is it?

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:13.960
Come in!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.280
Pardon me.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:20.040
The inspectors in town just
informed me that they saw

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.040
who they think was Niimi refer
to himself as Iori Tanaka

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.860
before entering a high-class restaurant

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:27.540
called Yamao in Gion-Shinchi.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:31.050
Souji, Saito, you up to this?

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:32.010
Sir!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.550
But of course.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:36.260
If we try apprehending him inside,

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.930
there is no need to take a large group.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.850
It’ll be just the four of us.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.060
I understand.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.570
Let’s hurry and get this over with.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:52.190
Yamao

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.740
Yamazaki, go around back.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:55.910
Yes, sir!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.160
Let’s go.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.220
The guests are growing
impatient in the stateroom.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.090
Hurry it up!

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:04.160
Sir!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.580
Welcome to--

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:08.720
Th-there a problem, sir?

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.300
Where are you serving
your guest Iori Tanaka?!

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:12.680
I-I wouldn’t know!

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:13.550
Passin’ through!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.190
Commander, let’s go.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:20.100
Wh-who are you?!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:22.100
Vulgar cretin!

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.100
What’s all that ruckus?

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:29.980
What are you doin’?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.320
H-Hijikata!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:34.490
So you were here!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:37.990
What are you doing in a
place like this, Niimi-san?

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.460
Why are you here?

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.940
If-if something were to happen to me,

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:45.590
S-Serizawa-sensei will let you have it!

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:47.960
Serizawa-sensei will?

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.740
Did Serizawa-san order you to give that

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:52.900
medicine to national loyalists?

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.010
Who are these brutes?!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.550
The Shinsengumi.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.510
What?! They’re Mibu Wolves?

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.230
Really, now.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.890
There was no need to rush to your death.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:12.650
Damn you!

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.720
You’re a bunch of
fools who don’t grasp

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.250
the political situation at hand!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.170
You won’t get off lightly
if you try to harm me.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.540
Is that all you have to say?

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:28.660
What?!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.310
Hajime-kun, up!

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.540
Souji!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.700
You’re slow; too slow!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.080
Your strikes are like that of a child!

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:10.580
You kept your wits, even
after becoming a fury?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.260
Remember what I said?

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:15.460
“You won’t get off lightly
if you try to harm me.”

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.680
This ticks me off.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.310
It’s like he has the upper hand even

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:22.910
though there are three of us.

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:24.970
This isn’t funny.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.230
This is the power of a fury!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.880
The new era will be

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:32.480
handed over to whosoever
possesses this medicine!

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.570
Choshu, Satsuma and even Tosa...

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.930
Everyone desperately wanted it!

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:40.990
So who did you sell it to?

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:45.490
Those men presented a tasty proposition,

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.540
but you made that a thing of the past!

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.430
You’re hardly a match for me!

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:10.930
Blood...

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:14.940
Blood! It’s blood!

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:20.870
Blood. Give me blood!

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.360
Blood! There’s blood!

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:24.830
Blood!

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:46.600
Hijikata-san, what brings
you here? It’s so late.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.100
Is Serizawa-san in?

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:52.620
He’s in, but it looks
like he went to bed.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:55.830
If you need him, I think you
should wait till tomorrow.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.370
All right.

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:01.110
Then I want you to tell him for me.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.620
Niimi-san committed honorable suicide.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:13.620
Headquarters of the Kyoto Military Commissioner
Konkaikoumyouji Main Temple

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.030
Okay, I understand.

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:19.630
You handled this incident
with the Water of Life well.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.440
However, some of the responsibility

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:24.880
for this fiasco lies with Serizawa.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.430
How have you dealt with
him since we last talked?

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:31.400
Sir, I am currently persuading
him to relinquish

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.640
his position as chief.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.240
That is not what I meant!
You still don’t get it?

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:39.990
I am saying that if you are to
manage the patrols around Kyoto,

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:43.300
I want the two of you to personally
lead the Shinsengumi!

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.990
Do not make me spell it out any clearer!

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.660
You may leave for today.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.690
Yes, sir!

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:30.340
You think you can kill me?

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:32.340
What a hilarious joke!

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:35.980
For the Shinsengumi, I
will commit any crime...

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:39.390
I will even become a devil from Hell!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.400
The Great Dawn
